{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Performance","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","text":"The binary-size budget","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each store their running ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a private ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, read by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every one of those ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s captures ","type":"text"},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a ","type":"text"},{"code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In practice, a completed ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"running","type":"text"}]},{"text":" operation: without ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the rest of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" safety net this guarantee supports.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"text":" only ever go active once ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)"},{"text":" have confirmed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":" is already ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" — both fall back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"text":" can never be observed alongside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refreshError":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/refresherror","type":"topic","title":"refreshError","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refreshError"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error from the most recently failed "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is left untouched by a refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type"